# TASK-AI-169 — root cause: run-ledger duplicates the ledger that work-guard already owns

WHERE: tools/ai-brain/run-ledger.js (whole file: admit :115, record :203/:453, isPlaceholder migration, own goal rollups, maskCredentials :16).
WRONG: 60 rounds of findings all come from run-ledger keeping a SECOND budget model on the same file as work-guard's ProgressLedger (merged in #503): placeholder migration moves exhausted budget between items; goal rollups race with work-guard's totals; `__proto__` item ids hit a plain object; regex URL masking misses `HTTPS://user:pass@`.
GOAL (Work Item TASK-AI-169 "one budget ledger and execution chain"): run-ledger is a THIN adapter over ProgressLedger (tools/ai-brain/work-guard.js, PASSed, do NOT edit):

- admission/caps/attempt counting/goal totals = call ProgressLedger reserve/record/admit only; delete isPlaceholder, migration, and any separate items/goals counters in run-ledger.
- run-ledger only adds the execution-chain metadata (writer→review→repair links, layer, verdict) stored under its own key that the validator ignores, keyed with Object.create(null) or a Map, rejecting `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` ids.
- credential masking: parse with `new URL()` (scheme case-insensitive) and blank username/password; fall back to a case-insensitive regex for non-URL strings.
  Expect the file to SHRINK substantially.
  VERIFY: existing run-ledger tests stay green (rewrite ones that asserted the removed placeholder behaviour); add tests for the 4 reviewer scenarios above (item A/B same attempt id cap=1 → B refused or A still exhausted; late goal rollup counted once; `HTTPS://user:pass123@…` masked; `__proto__` item id refused). Run node --test tools/ai-brain/test/run-ledger.test.js tools/ai-brain/test/work-guard.test.js, pnpm test:brain, pnpm format:check, pnpm run security:secrets.

