- fast-redact (latest 3.x): `pnpm add -w fast-redact` for masking route endpoints/credentials in ledger metadata, with an explicit path allowlist; plus `new URL()` for userinfo. Delete the custom regex masking.

- REUSE FIRST (operator 04/11): before writing any parser, sanitizer/redactor, URL/state sync, network guard, retry/queue, date/money/format helper or UI widget, search for a maintained library or an attached repo (manifest, context7.js, npm/GitHub) and USE it. Hand-write only if none fits, and say why in .oc/tools-used.txt ("no-lib: <reason>"). New dependencies are allowed when they are well-maintained (recent release, real user base, OSI licence), pinned to an exact version with the lockfile committed; never for auth/tenant/money logic without the Work Item naming it.

## root-cause (reference implementation, 04/11) — adapt, do not invent
Design reference (Python, read only): github.com/arieradle/shekel (per-run budget context, warn at threshold, raise at cap, tool-call counting) and github.com/darshjme/agent-budget (multi-scope per-session caps, thread-safe). Mirror their single-owner budget model: ONE ledger owner (our ProgressLedger) and thin wrappers; no second counter set.
Clone read-only to C:/Users/gumac/AI/ref/<name> (git clone --depth 1), read the named parts, adapt to our files; respect licence and credit the source in a header comment; log reference + what was adapted in .oc/tools-used.txt.

## root-cause (USE THE PACKAGE, 04/11 12:10) — masking
`fast-redact@3.5.0` (MIT) is on npm: `pnpm add -w fast-redact@3.5.0`. Use it for ledger metadata masking with an explicit path list (e.g. ['*.endpoint','*.headers.authorization','*.apiKey','*.token']), plus `new URL()` to blank username/password in endpoint strings. Delete the hand-written regex masking. The ledger itself stays a thin adapter over ProgressLedger (sections above).
